<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Barlow half year shr below expectations.</title>
<headline>Barlow half year shr below expectations.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-excepts (cts) 145.4	vs 142.5</p>
<p>    Shr, net (cts)	   158.5	vs 146.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  36	   vs 33</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters expected pre-exceptional earnings per share in a range of 150 to 165 cents with consensus figure at 160.7 cents. The dividend was seen in a 36.0 to 38.0 cents range, averaging at 37.1.</p>
</text>
